{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>YHWH</b> — the meaning is true: He is slow to anger and great in strength. The meaning is doubled by way of analogy: like a man who has great strength, he then masters his anger. And so it is written in the Torah: \"And now, let the strength of YHWH grow great,\" and after it is written: \"YHWH, slow to anger.\" And even though He lengthens [His patience] for the wicked, He does not acquit them." "<b>and in the storm</b> — a metaphor for swiftness in the wind of the storm." "<b>and a cloud is the dust of His feet</b> — a metaphor for the running of the clouds. And the meaning: concerning the decrees that come from heaven swiftly, for they are above the clouds."], :book :nahum, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Nahum -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/nachum"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:14:29.752910858Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}